00:43:14.030 --> 00:43:15.380
I'd love to meet you, Jazzy Jeff.

00:43:15.380 --> 00:43:17.420
I named my dog after you.

00:43:17.420 --> 00:43:20.810
But I also named him after Jeff Probst.

00:43:20.810 --> 00:43:24.930
The best host in the
history of television.

00:43:24.930 --> 00:43:26.410
- You have to land on one thing

00:43:26.410 --> 00:43:27.770
that you call the dog though.

00:43:27.770 --> 00:43:29.130
The dog has a name-

00:43:29.130 --> 00:43:31.660
- Jasper DJ Jazzy Jeff Probst.

00:43:31.660 --> 00:43:33.760
- You can't call your dog multiple things.

00:43:35.140 --> 00:43:36.931
- When we train him, we call him Jasper.

00:43:36.931 --> 00:43:38.040
- (laughs) Okay.

00:43:38.040 --> 00:43:41.810
So when he is expected to
do something, he is Jasper.

00:43:41.810 --> 00:43:45.250
In any other circumstance,
he's something else.

00:43:45.250 --> 00:43:46.083
- Yeah.

00:43:46.083 --> 00:43:47.090
And look, you can move, or I can mop

00:43:47.090 --> 00:43:47.950
the floor with this guy.

00:43:47.950 --> 00:43:50.600
- He's kinda like a Smithsonian exhibit.

00:43:50.600 --> 00:43:52.250
The way you can just kinda
manipulate him like that.

00:43:52.250 --> 00:43:53.083
- Yeah, I know.

00:43:53.083 --> 00:43:54.870
See, and this is what I wanted.

00:43:54.870 --> 00:43:57.060
And this is what you get
with this type of dog.

00:43:57.060 --> 00:43:59.410
It's like, well, I'm just gonna stay here.

00:43:59.410 --> 00:44:01.420
He's a love sponge, man.

00:44:01.420 --> 00:44:04.730
And he's got this thing we call the face.

00:44:04.730 --> 00:44:06.370
Have you seen this?

00:44:06.370 --> 00:44:08.160
When he's excited.

00:44:08.160 --> 00:44:11.070
So when I come home, he still barks

00:44:11.070 --> 00:44:12.653
until he realizes it's me.

00:44:14.345 --> 00:44:16.380
And this is why we think
this is a Pomeranian thing

00:44:16.380 --> 00:44:18.086
unless he's not Pomeranian,

00:44:18.086 --> 00:44:18.919
and then whatever part he is.

00:44:18.919 --> 00:44:19.880
This is where this comes from,

00:44:19.880 --> 00:44:22.180
'cause Jade doesn't do this.

00:44:22.180 --> 00:44:24.890
He will snarl his lips.

00:44:24.890 --> 00:44:26.040
- [Rhett] Like a smile a little bit?

00:44:26.040 --> 00:44:29.143
- He'll snarl his lips and
move his jaw like this.

00:44:31.150 --> 00:44:34.713
When he gets excited, he's
doing this with his lips.

00:44:36.680 --> 00:44:40.350
And we call it the face
and we don't like it.

00:44:40.350 --> 00:44:42.510
So we always tell him,
"Don't do the face."

00:44:42.510 --> 00:44:44.590
- Well, I'm gonna tell you right now.

00:44:44.590 --> 00:44:46.170
He doesn't get his long
legs from a Pomeranian.

00:44:46.170 --> 00:44:47.003
That's what I thought.

00:44:47.003 --> 00:44:48.700
That's what a Pomeranian looks like.

00:44:48.700 --> 00:44:49.840
- Well, there's a big mane.

00:44:49.840 --> 00:44:51.753
Under that mane, aren't
there like, long legs?

00:44:51.753 --> 00:44:53.960
- That's not that long.

00:44:53.960 --> 00:44:55.290
These are really long legs.

00:44:55.290 --> 00:44:56.680
- Yeah, he's something else.

00:44:56.680 --> 00:44:58.533
- Here, look, here's
a Pomeranian with a...

00:44:58.533 --> 00:44:59.750
- A fake leg.

00:44:59.750 --> 00:45:01.820
- A prosthetic wooden leg.

00:45:01.820 --> 00:45:04.186
- Oh man. Jasper.

00:45:04.186 --> 00:45:05.170
That could be cool.

00:45:05.170 --> 00:45:07.160
- But he could be part of that

00:45:07.160 --> 00:45:09.883
because his, I mean,
his face is that color.

00:45:11.080 --> 00:45:14.110
- His face is the same as Jade's.

00:45:14.110 --> 00:45:17.160
I mean, he's definitely
got some dachshund in him.

00:45:17.160 --> 00:45:20.040
Long hair dachshund, but I don't know

00:45:20.040 --> 00:45:22.070
what the other thing is.

00:45:22.070 --> 00:45:26.130
I mean, doing the genetic
analysis is something that-

00:45:26.130 --> 00:45:27.711
- You should do it.

00:45:27.711 --> 00:45:29.490
- Just because it's fun to know.

00:45:29.490 --> 00:45:31.390
- I mean, 'cause like a
real long haired dachshund

00:45:31.390 --> 00:45:34.050
has those really long ears.

00:45:34.050 --> 00:45:36.860
And both Jade and him have...

00:45:36.860 --> 00:45:38.360
- Shorter ears.
- The short ears.

00:45:38.360 --> 00:45:39.460
It comes from something.

00:45:39.460 --> 00:45:41.400
- Yeah, we'll have to figure that out.

00:45:41.400 --> 00:45:43.890
But the thing that I've noticed

00:45:43.890 --> 00:45:47.733
in including him in the family is,

00:45:48.790 --> 00:45:50.110
I think I've gone...

00:45:53.472 --> 00:45:56.530
Well, I thought I was a
dog person because of Jade,

00:45:56.530 --> 00:45:58.750
but I think I was just a Jade person.

00:45:58.750 --> 00:46:02.210
Like, I like dogs a lot more

00:46:02.210 --> 00:46:04.790
but I've noticed now that Jasper's there

00:46:04.790 --> 00:46:07.590
and we're like going
through training again

00:46:07.590 --> 00:46:12.300
and trying to get him to cooperate
and learn and understand.

00:46:12.300 --> 00:46:15.750
It's like, there's a
reward associated with that

00:46:15.750 --> 00:46:16.940
that I hadn't experienced

00:46:16.940 --> 00:46:19.790
because I didn't train
Jade that much at all.

00:46:19.790 --> 00:46:22.370
And I'm not training him that much.

00:46:22.370 --> 00:46:25.900
But even a little bit of
obedience, it's very rewarding.

00:46:25.900 --> 00:46:27.680
And I start to feel like I'm moving

00:46:27.680 --> 00:46:31.933
from being a Jade lover to
actually being a dog lover.

00:46:33.500 --> 00:46:36.200
But Jade will always be my number one.

00:46:36.200 --> 00:46:40.310
We started watching this show about dogs

00:46:40.310 --> 00:46:41.530
because he started getting into it.

00:46:41.530 --> 00:46:44.520
And there's this like
grooming competition show.

00:46:44.520 --> 00:46:46.260
It's absolutely obnoxious.

00:46:46.260 --> 00:46:48.120
I can't even remember the name of it.

00:46:48.120 --> 00:46:49.610
I couldn't get through a whole episode

00:46:49.610 --> 00:46:52.960
because the pilot episode,
it was just obnoxious.

00:46:52.960 --> 00:46:54.943
But the competition was,

00:46:57.000 --> 00:46:59.970
these groomers were given a dog

00:46:59.970 --> 00:47:03.910
that looked like what they
called their heart dog,

00:47:03.910 --> 00:47:08.500
which is like the first dog
that won their heart over.

00:47:08.500 --> 00:47:09.770
So for me, that's Jade.

00:47:09.770 --> 00:47:11.280
Jade is my heart dog.

00:47:11.280 --> 00:47:13.350
I assume Barbara is going
to be your heart dog.

00:47:13.350 --> 00:47:15.870
You won't really know
until you get another dog.

00:47:15.870 --> 00:47:17.330
Because all of these people,

00:47:17.330 --> 00:47:19.130
their heart dogs had passed away.

00:47:19.130 --> 00:47:21.300
And now they still love dogs

00:47:21.300 --> 00:47:22.660
and they groom 'em and stuff like that.

00:47:22.660 --> 00:47:24.010
But they have this special attachment

00:47:24.010 --> 00:47:27.590
to this one dog that
connected with their heart.

00:47:27.590 --> 00:47:29.450
And so they brought out these dogs

00:47:29.450 --> 00:47:32.500
that looked like their heart dog,

00:47:32.500 --> 00:47:34.930
'cause they would show a
picture of, this is so-and-so.

00:47:34.930 --> 00:47:37.550
He died in 1986.

00:47:37.550 --> 00:47:39.860
And then, but I'm gonna groom
this dog to look like him.

00:47:39.860 --> 00:47:43.013
And then they're in tears
grooming these dogs.

00:47:43.013 --> 00:47:44.253
- What is this on?

00:47:45.800 --> 00:47:47.530
- One of the streamers.

00:47:47.530 --> 00:47:49.063
Netflix maybe. I don't know.

00:47:51.720 --> 00:47:53.190
But the thing that I
couldn't help but notice

00:47:53.190 --> 00:47:55.653
is that none of the dogs-

00:47:55.653 --> 00:47:57.350
- Looked like the heart dogs.
- Looked like the heart dog,

00:47:57.350 --> 00:48:01.150
yet these people were still bawling.

00:48:01.150 --> 00:48:06.150
Like, doesn't he look
just like my munchkin?

00:48:06.300 --> 00:48:07.970
And I'm like, "No, he doesn't."

00:48:07.970 --> 00:48:10.841
But I think there's like
some sort of blindness.

00:48:10.841 --> 00:48:15.841
- I mean, first of all, I'm a dog person

00:48:16.120 --> 00:48:17.820
and I've always been a dog person.

00:48:19.930 --> 00:48:24.930
But without a doubt connected
much more with Barbara

00:48:25.860 --> 00:48:28.560
than any other dog that I've ever had.

00:48:28.560 --> 00:48:32.950
If for no other reason
than Barbara's been around

00:48:32.950 --> 00:48:36.400
for like what, five years now.

00:48:36.400 --> 00:48:38.598
- But she's also your first indoor dog.

00:48:38.598 --> 00:48:39.707
- No, no.

00:48:40.870 --> 00:48:42.670
We had Murl and Gypsy.

00:48:42.670 --> 00:48:43.890
- Oh, that's right. That's right.

00:48:43.890 --> 00:48:47.183
- But both of them died within a year.

00:48:48.370 --> 00:48:49.820
If you've read the "Book of Mythicality"

00:48:49.820 --> 00:48:52.923
you know the dog curse.

00:48:56.890 --> 00:48:58.983
But it's interesting because,

00:49:00.120 --> 00:49:05.120
I mean, first of all, Jessie
for the entire pandemic

00:49:05.470 --> 00:49:10.470
has been, every couple of
nights, she's on the couch,

00:49:10.880 --> 00:49:12.840
she's going through the adoption websites.

00:49:12.840 --> 00:49:16.880
Like she is big, let's get a second dog.

00:49:16.880 --> 00:49:19.010
Jasper, he sheds more than Jade,

00:49:19.010 --> 00:49:20.510
'cause I'm seeing his hair go around

00:49:20.510 --> 00:49:21.910
and that's why I'm sneezing.

00:49:24.500 --> 00:49:27.930
Here's the thing, I'm not
opposed to a second dog.

00:49:27.930 --> 00:49:32.220
I know for a fact that I would...

00:49:32.220 --> 00:49:34.670
You see those classic
TikToks, which I think,

00:49:34.670 --> 00:49:38.010
you kind of represent the
classic dad situation,

00:49:38.010 --> 00:49:40.480
which is like, a dad
who's completely opposed

00:49:40.480 --> 00:49:43.610
to getting a dog, doesn't
think he likes dogs.

00:49:43.610 --> 00:49:45.774
I mean, I've seen like a hundred TikToks

00:49:45.774 --> 00:49:47.617
where it's just like dad saying,

00:49:47.617 --> 00:49:49.210
"You're gonna have to
take care of this thing."

00:49:49.210 --> 00:49:51.020
And then cut to, they play the song

00:49:51.020 --> 00:49:52.220
and it's this dad doing

00:49:52.220 --> 00:49:53.634
what you're doing with the dog.

00:49:53.634 --> 00:49:54.870
And it's like, it's a trope at this point,

00:49:54.870 --> 00:49:57.600
but that's not me.

00:49:57.600 --> 00:50:01.180
I knew that I was going to be sickeningly

00:50:01.180 --> 00:50:04.630
in love with Barbara, say
embarrassing things to her

00:50:04.630 --> 00:50:06.040
that sometimes my wife tweets

00:50:06.040 --> 00:50:07.890
about what I say to Barbara.

00:50:07.890 --> 00:50:09.490
Barbara is my mistress.

00:50:09.490 --> 00:50:11.580
She's my girlfriend.

00:50:11.580 --> 00:50:13.660
I'm completely in love with her.

00:50:13.660 --> 00:50:17.570
And I do want another dog and...

00:50:18.700 --> 00:50:21.397
Or I'm open to another dog.

00:50:21.397 --> 00:50:22.930
And I don't feel like
it would be this thing

00:50:22.930 --> 00:50:24.160
where it's just like,

00:50:24.160 --> 00:50:26.423
oh, this dog is replacing Barbara.

00:50:28.550 --> 00:50:32.630
I'm so happy and content with Barbara

00:50:32.630 --> 00:50:36.284
that I don't feel a need for another dog.

00:50:36.284 --> 00:50:38.160
And the thought of the initial

00:50:38.160 --> 00:50:40.527
sort of like process of training and...

00:50:40.527 --> 00:50:42.750
And first of all, my kids aren't
gonna do anything helpful.

00:50:42.750 --> 00:50:45.060
My kids don't help at all
when it comes to this stuff.

00:50:45.060 --> 00:50:47.100
Are they saying that they
also want a dog though?

00:50:47.100 --> 00:50:48.090
- Of course they want a dog,

00:50:48.090 --> 00:50:50.870
because they don't have to do
anything except play with it.

00:50:50.870 --> 00:50:52.160
- Yeah. It wouldn't be theirs.

00:50:52.160 --> 00:50:55.660
- It would be on me and
Jessie to do the stuff

00:50:55.660 --> 00:50:57.913
to make it a good dog.

00:50:58.780 --> 00:51:01.960
And I'm just like, I don't know.

00:51:01.960 --> 00:51:03.393
I could easily be broken down.

00:51:03.393 --> 00:51:05.690
This is not some giant barrier.

00:51:05.690 --> 00:51:08.200
- If you went home today and
there was a dog, you would...

00:51:08.200 --> 00:51:09.360
- I'd be super happy.

00:51:09.360 --> 00:51:10.960
- So is it really, Jessie's not,

00:51:12.139 --> 00:51:13.400
she doesn't know if she's ready.

00:51:13.400 --> 00:51:16.083
- Well, there's complicating
factors with us.

00:51:17.000 --> 00:51:19.170
I don't think we could
have Jasper in the house

00:51:19.170 --> 00:51:21.220
because I would be sneezing all the time.

00:51:24.170 --> 00:51:25.950
I know there's controversy over this

00:51:25.950 --> 00:51:28.563
but hypoallergenic is a thing.

00:51:29.450 --> 00:51:32.900
There are dogs that are less
prone to give you allergies.

00:51:32.900 --> 00:51:34.700
And they're the ones that
have hair rather than fur,

00:51:34.700 --> 00:51:36.190
and I don't know what Barbara is.

00:51:36.190 --> 00:51:37.720
She's a mix of some kind.

00:51:37.720 --> 00:51:40.510
But she doesn't cause me to start sneezing

00:51:40.510 --> 00:51:41.600
when I hang out with her.

00:51:41.600 --> 00:51:45.240
So we would need to get a dog
that fits in that category.

00:51:45.240 --> 00:51:47.740
But yet we would want to adopt a dog

00:51:47.740 --> 00:51:50.030
versus go to a breeder.

00:51:50.030 --> 00:51:52.080
So it's like, it kinda complicates

00:51:52.080 --> 00:51:54.630
and makes our decision a
little bit more difficult.

00:51:57.014 --> 00:51:59.320
But an interesting thing
is, I don't have any desire

00:51:59.320 --> 00:52:02.520
for my next dog to look like Barbara,

00:52:02.520 --> 00:52:07.520
but I am very interested in
the disposition being the same.

00:52:08.060 --> 00:52:11.570
- Once you get used to
one kind, it's easier.

00:52:11.570 --> 00:52:13.030
You know what you're dealing with.

00:52:13.030 --> 00:52:14.483
It lets you get a baseline.

00:52:16.210 --> 00:52:18.930
- I don't have...

00:52:18.930 --> 00:52:22.224
The fact that it takes a lot for,

00:52:22.224 --> 00:52:25.080
it took a lot for Jade and
it takes more for Jasper

00:52:25.080 --> 00:52:26.780
to warm up to people.

00:52:26.780 --> 00:52:29.173
And that feels like
more of a project to me.

00:52:30.360 --> 00:52:31.820
I don't think Jessie has a lot of capacity

00:52:31.820 --> 00:52:34.320
for a project dog.

00:52:34.320 --> 00:52:37.470
It's more just like, I
mean, I love Barbara,

00:52:37.470 --> 00:52:39.620
but I do understand that
if Barbara were to go

00:52:39.620 --> 00:52:42.070
to an Airbnb where somebody else lived

00:52:42.070 --> 00:52:43.517
and then we forgot her and left her there

00:52:43.517 --> 00:52:44.850
and the other family came home,

00:52:44.850 --> 00:52:46.350
she would immediately acclimate

00:52:46.350 --> 00:52:48.440
and love them just as
much as she loves us.

00:52:48.440 --> 00:52:53.440
Like, she is a endless supply
of attention and cuddling,

00:52:54.160 --> 00:52:57.463
but it is not exclusive to us.

00:52:58.530 --> 00:53:01.060
- I actually saw it as an advantage to,

00:53:01.060 --> 00:53:04.550
almost a download Jasper at 11 months old,

00:53:04.550 --> 00:53:06.810
to adopt him at that age,

00:53:06.810 --> 00:53:11.340
because yeah, you get the
cuteness of the puppy,

00:53:11.340 --> 00:53:14.750
but at least I thought, I mean,

00:53:14.750 --> 00:53:17.227
there's a lot more
training that goes into it.

00:53:17.227 --> 00:53:19.390
And we were told that he was housebroken.

00:53:19.390 --> 00:53:22.530
We also knew that if he's part dachshund,

00:53:22.530 --> 00:53:25.010
that like, he's still
gonna sneak off and poop

00:53:25.010 --> 00:53:26.480
for the next three years.

00:53:26.480 --> 00:53:27.420
- Eat a little cat shit here and there.

00:53:27.420 --> 00:53:28.333
- Yeah, that too.

00:53:29.620 --> 00:53:32.790
But what we didn't know
was that, okay, you give up

00:53:32.790 --> 00:53:36.600
all of the puppy learning curve
and you lose the cuteness,

00:53:36.600 --> 00:53:40.130
you get more of the dog that
you know you're gonna be with,

00:53:40.130 --> 00:53:42.040
but you also get some sort of,

00:53:42.040 --> 00:53:44.450
if there's any emotional baggage or trauma

00:53:44.450 --> 00:53:45.540
or something like that.

00:53:45.540 --> 00:53:47.340
Like, his separation anxiety

00:53:47.340 --> 00:53:48.870
is something that we're dealing with.

00:53:48.870 --> 00:53:52.650
And if Christy's goes
out in the front yard

00:53:52.650 --> 00:53:55.860
and leaves him in the house,
he's barking and howling.

00:53:55.860 --> 00:53:57.517
And like I said, I'm
doing some crate training

00:53:57.517 --> 00:53:58.857
to get him better at that.

00:53:58.857 --> 00:54:01.060
And you know, in a few months,

00:54:01.060 --> 00:54:02.950
I'm sure he'll be a lot better.

00:54:02.950 --> 00:54:06.350
But I think ultimately I'm glad

00:54:06.350 --> 00:54:08.650
that we got a dog that
was a little bit older.

00:54:10.405 --> 00:54:12.520
And Christy is so attached to him

00:54:12.520 --> 00:54:17.010
because he needs her so much
that like, she just loves it.

00:54:17.010 --> 00:54:18.650
She just eats it up.

00:54:18.650 --> 00:54:20.400
And she's like, I mean, she'll say,

00:54:21.437 --> 00:54:23.827
"I didn't save him. He saved me."

00:54:25.040 --> 00:54:27.700
And I'm like, "Christy, are you doing

00:54:27.700 --> 00:54:28.840
what's best for the dog?

00:54:28.840 --> 00:54:32.570
Like, you really, you cuddle him so much,

00:54:32.570 --> 00:54:34.900
that like, that's not really helping

00:54:34.900 --> 00:54:36.820
with the separation anxiety."

00:54:36.820 --> 00:54:40.090
You know, it's like, I mean,
she doesn't take a shower

00:54:40.090 --> 00:54:44.350
with the dog and we do get
him in the crate now for that.

00:54:44.350 --> 00:54:49.080
But yeah, for a while I was
like, "Are you making him worse

00:54:49.080 --> 00:54:51.030
because it makes you feel that much better

00:54:51.030 --> 00:54:51.863
that he needs you so much?

00:54:51.863 --> 00:54:53.860
- Are you saying this is
like a Munchhausen situation?

00:54:53.860 --> 00:54:55.610
Or however you say that?

00:54:55.610 --> 00:54:57.890
- I don't really know what that is

00:54:57.890 --> 00:54:59.057
enough to agree or not.

00:54:59.057 --> 00:55:01.883
- That's when, not to make light of it.

00:55:01.883 --> 00:55:04.000
This is a real thing that happens.

00:55:04.000 --> 00:55:08.250
So it's when a parent
purposely keeps a child sick

00:55:08.250 --> 00:55:09.851
so the child is dependent upon them.

00:55:09.851 --> 00:55:10.684
- Oh my God.

00:55:10.684 --> 00:55:12.810
- It's like the little
girl in "Sixth Sense"

00:55:12.810 --> 00:55:16.860
that is under the bed and yeah.

00:55:16.860 --> 00:55:18.650
I mean, this happens all the time.

00:55:18.650 --> 00:55:20.880
It's like, this kid is
being constantly like,

00:55:20.880 --> 00:55:22.640
usually they're poisoning the kid

00:55:22.640 --> 00:55:25.180
or doing something to keep the kid sick,

00:55:25.180 --> 00:55:27.230
because it creates this
co-dependent relationship

00:55:27.230 --> 00:55:28.810
that makes the parent feel

00:55:28.810 --> 00:55:31.850
like they've got some self-worth.

00:55:31.850 --> 00:55:34.065
So you think your wife is
doing that with your dog?

00:55:34.065 --> 00:55:34.898
(laughs)

00:55:34.898 --> 00:55:36.586
- Yeah, she's definitely
poisoning the dog.

00:55:36.586 --> 00:55:37.419
No.

00:55:37.419 --> 00:55:39.670
- She's the one who...

00:55:39.670 --> 00:55:40.700
That wasn't cat shit.

00:55:40.700 --> 00:55:44.920
That was something Christy
made and said it was cat shit.

00:55:44.920 --> 00:55:45.753
- Okay. Yeah.

00:55:45.753 --> 00:55:46.720
It seems like Christy and I have something

00:55:46.720 --> 00:55:49.100
to talk about tonight.

00:55:49.100 --> 00:55:49.933
Okay.

00:55:49.933 --> 00:55:52.270
So we got another member of the family.

00:55:52.270 --> 00:55:53.330
I don't regret it.

00:55:53.330 --> 00:55:55.430
I'm actually feeling pretty good about it.

00:55:56.430 --> 00:55:59.195
And I think he's feeling good about it.

00:55:59.195 --> 00:56:01.650
He's loving everybody in the house

00:56:01.650 --> 00:56:03.960
and he doesn't hate you anymore.

00:56:03.960 --> 00:56:05.320
He's just barking at you.

00:56:05.320 --> 00:56:09.660
- Yeah, I think the cool
thing about a dog like Jasper

00:56:09.660 --> 00:56:12.700
is that there is a...

00:56:15.250 --> 00:56:17.130
He presents a challenge.

00:56:17.130 --> 00:56:18.960
He just picked something off the ground.

00:56:18.960 --> 00:56:20.823
- He tastes a lot of things.

00:56:22.893 --> 00:56:24.350
- And it's a challenge that,

00:56:24.350 --> 00:56:27.334
I'm okay with that challenge
if it's my friend's dog.

00:56:27.334 --> 00:56:28.167
(laughs)

00:56:28.167 --> 00:56:29.000
You know what I'm saying?

00:56:29.000 --> 00:56:32.590
It's like, I'm trying to
get Jasper to warm up to me.

00:56:32.590 --> 00:56:35.630
And one day he will, like
Jade used to bark at me

00:56:35.630 --> 00:56:38.860
and now Jade wants to lick
me every time I see her.

00:56:38.860 --> 00:56:43.140
It's just the process of making
that transformation happen

00:56:43.140 --> 00:56:44.320
is something that I don't know

00:56:44.320 --> 00:56:47.220
if I have the patience for my own dog.

00:56:47.220 --> 00:56:48.950
So I'm happy for you to do the work

00:56:48.950 --> 00:56:50.060
and me to experience the benefit.

00:56:50.060 --> 00:56:50.950
- I think you should do it.

00:56:50.950 --> 00:56:52.820
I think you need to get another Barbara.

00:56:52.820 --> 00:56:54.330
- Well, you know what we did?

00:56:54.330 --> 00:56:56.180
It's funny, we went through
this phase with Barbara

00:56:56.180 --> 00:56:58.863
where I was so sure,

00:57:00.600 --> 00:57:04.790
like, I was talking seriously
about cloning Barbara.

00:57:04.790 --> 00:57:06.090
- You loved her that much.

00:57:08.150 --> 00:57:09.360
It's not that I love her less.

00:57:09.360 --> 00:57:13.370
It was that I hadn't had
a dog in a long time,

00:57:13.370 --> 00:57:15.230
hadn't had a dog that I had connected with

00:57:15.230 --> 00:57:17.360
to the degree that we've
connected with Barbara.

00:57:17.360 --> 00:57:19.920
Began to believe that maybe
the dog curse was over,

00:57:19.920 --> 00:57:21.610
especially when she got out

00:57:21.610 --> 00:57:24.070
and literally left the house
and jumped into somebody,

00:57:24.070 --> 00:57:27.480
a stranger's car and
still came back to us.

00:57:27.480 --> 00:57:30.650
At that point, I was like,
okay, maybe the curse is broken.

00:57:30.650 --> 00:57:33.300
And we started to think like,

00:57:33.300 --> 00:57:35.940
oh, what if we always had
this little white dog?

00:57:35.940 --> 00:57:37.550
We always called her Barbara.

00:57:37.550 --> 00:57:39.100
'cause there are people who do this.

00:57:39.100 --> 00:57:40.272
And it was just like,

00:57:40.272 --> 00:57:42.120
let's just do this for the rest of time.

00:57:42.120 --> 00:57:44.310
You know, the price of cloning a dog

00:57:44.310 --> 00:57:46.723
is dropping every year.

00:57:48.580 --> 00:57:50.573
And then I was like, that's crazy.

00:57:51.440 --> 00:57:53.050
I mean, I was like, that's crazy

00:57:53.050 --> 00:57:56.940
and also insisting on it being Barbara

00:57:56.940 --> 00:57:57.910
and looking like Barbara.

00:57:57.910 --> 00:57:58.820
No offense to you.

00:57:58.820 --> 00:58:00.810
I was like, I feel like I'm giving in

00:58:00.810 --> 00:58:02.452
to some unhealthy tendency.

00:58:02.452 --> 00:58:05.029
- I'm not gonna clone Jade,

00:58:05.029 --> 00:58:06.529
but I do still think about it.

00:58:08.045 --> 00:58:08.878
- I let go of that,

00:58:08.878 --> 00:58:11.020
and I know that I'll love
the next dog as much.

00:58:11.020 --> 00:58:12.050
Jessie wants-

00:58:12.050 --> 00:58:14.790
- I just wanted Jade to not be threatened.

00:58:14.790 --> 00:58:17.520
I didn't want a new dog
to get more attention.

00:58:17.520 --> 00:58:19.820
So. I didn't want an upgrade.

00:58:19.820 --> 00:58:22.400
'cause I thought Jade
could pick up on that.

00:58:22.400 --> 00:58:24.920
I wanted Jade to stay the queen.

00:58:24.920 --> 00:58:26.510
And she's still my dog.

00:58:26.510 --> 00:58:27.890
Now this is Christy's dog,

00:58:27.890 --> 00:58:29.340
and Jade is still the best.

00:58:29.340 --> 00:58:31.240
- Well, the thing that Jessie keeps saying

00:58:31.240 --> 00:58:32.490
is that she doesn't want there,

00:58:32.490 --> 00:58:34.300
she wants there to be a crossover

00:58:34.300 --> 00:58:37.317
between Barbara and the next dog.

00:58:37.317 --> 00:58:39.710
And so why not begin the process now?

00:58:39.710 --> 00:58:41.190
- Yeah. You're talking
about lifespan here.

00:58:41.190 --> 00:58:43.390
- Yeah, she's like the
idea of Barbara dying

00:58:43.390 --> 00:58:45.560
and then going through this grieving phase

00:58:45.560 --> 00:58:48.090
and then finding another dog,

00:58:48.090 --> 00:58:49.690
which I think there's an
argument to be made there.

00:58:49.690 --> 00:58:52.563
But Barbara is only five years old.

00:58:53.420 --> 00:58:55.020
She's a little dog.

00:58:55.020 --> 00:58:58.480
She's gonna, probably at least be 12, 13,

00:58:58.480 --> 00:59:00.503
maybe significantly older, I don't know.

00:59:01.500 --> 00:59:02.333
I don't know.

00:59:02.333 --> 00:59:04.893
I'm sure we'll get
another dog at some point,

00:59:05.860 --> 00:59:07.190
and I'm sure I'll love it

00:59:07.190 --> 00:59:09.000
just as much as I love Barbara.

00:59:09.000 --> 00:59:10.720
I mean, well, maybe a little
bit less than Barbara.

00:59:10.720 --> 00:59:11.910
- A little bit less.

00:59:11.910 --> 00:59:13.100
- A little bit less than Barbara.

00:59:13.100 --> 00:59:16.180
- I don't think I'm ever gonna
love a dog as much as Jade.

00:59:16.180 --> 00:59:17.233
And I don't want to.

00:59:18.320 --> 00:59:19.550
I can give you a rec though.

00:59:19.550 --> 00:59:20.653
It's totally related.

00:59:21.820 --> 00:59:23.760
I said we were watching
that dog grooming show.

00:59:23.760 --> 00:59:25.950
The reason why Lando got me to watch that,

00:59:25.950 --> 00:59:27.100
'cause he thought I'd be into it,

00:59:27.100 --> 00:59:31.710
is because he had gotten
me into another show

00:59:31.710 --> 00:59:35.057
that I'm recommending called
"Canine Intervention."

00:59:35.057 --> 00:59:39.400
"Canine Intervention," it's
kind of like "Dog Whisperer,"

00:59:39.400 --> 00:59:40.980
if you're familiar with that show.

00:59:40.980 --> 00:59:43.440
But I actually haven't watched that show.

00:59:43.440 --> 00:59:45.200
- Cesar?
- Yeah, Cesar's show.

00:59:45.200 --> 00:59:46.930
But it's like, you got problem dogs

00:59:46.930 --> 00:59:50.220
that then this guy, I call him Jas.

00:59:50.220 --> 00:59:53.340
It's J-A-S, like short for Jason, maybe.

00:59:53.340 --> 00:59:56.592
But the way that he says
his name is like, Johs.

00:59:56.592 --> 00:59:57.795
- Okay, that's weird.

00:59:57.795 --> 00:59:59.680
That's a little weird.

00:59:59.680 --> 01:00:00.700
- They don't say his name enough

01:00:00.700 --> 01:00:02.320
for me to get it straight in my head.

01:00:02.320 --> 01:00:04.050
But it's this guy from Oakland

01:00:04.050 --> 01:00:08.080
who travels all around California

01:00:08.080 --> 01:00:10.130
and helps with troubled troubled dogs.

01:00:10.130 --> 01:00:12.820
And like, he's got this training facility.

01:00:12.820 --> 01:00:16.330
And the way they do these shows now,

01:00:16.330 --> 01:00:18.810
it's like, all right,
there's a story of these dogs

01:00:18.810 --> 01:00:23.810
and it's really compelling,
like tears in my eyes

01:00:24.500 --> 01:00:27.520
watching these dogs transform.

01:00:27.520 --> 01:00:28.930
That's the other thing
that made it click for me

01:00:28.930 --> 01:00:30.450
was like, I wanted to watch this show

01:00:30.450 --> 01:00:32.820
because I'm trying to help train Jasper.

01:00:32.820 --> 01:00:35.100
But then I'm connecting
to all these dog stories

01:00:35.100 --> 01:00:36.293
and I'm like weeping.

01:00:37.130 --> 01:00:38.750
It's a really good show.

01:00:38.750 --> 01:00:42.290
And then at the end, like
with all these reality shows,

01:00:42.290 --> 01:00:44.320
you see him back home with his family

01:00:44.320 --> 01:00:47.160
talking about like,
oh, they got a newborn.

01:00:47.160 --> 01:00:49.930
And then they got these
seemingly ferocious dogs

01:00:49.930 --> 01:00:53.330
that are just so well-trained
and all around the baby.

01:00:53.330 --> 01:00:55.520
And so you get to know their home life

01:00:55.520 --> 01:00:57.230
and his professional life.

01:00:57.230 --> 01:00:58.640
And he's just got such a-

01:00:58.640 --> 01:00:59.977
- It's called "Canine Intervention?"

01:00:59.977 --> 01:01:04.030
- "Canine Intervention,"
but it's super cool.

01:01:04.030 --> 01:01:05.240
I mean, the stories are really good.

01:01:05.240 --> 01:01:06.980
It's really well produced.

01:01:06.980 --> 01:01:09.210
And that's my rec.

01:01:09.210 --> 01:01:13.070
If you're into dogs, you
should definitely watch it

01:01:13.070 --> 01:01:16.230
because all of the stories
and transformations

01:01:16.230 --> 01:01:20.703
are inspirational and moving.

01:01:21.690 --> 01:01:23.080
- All right, "Canine Intervention?"

01:01:23.080 --> 01:01:24.420
- Yeah.

